Bug patch cheval26-weak-state, ported to libsignal v0.105.4 (b2a5c30f3245c1bcad04b27b1e752a38321c793d).

Derived from Signal Messenger's libsignal (https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal):
Copyright 2020-2026 Signal Messenger, LLC. SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
(full text: ../../../LICENSE). See ../../README.md.

Reverses upstream commit cd361186fba60c83186262d91b03af608fb8c7c3 ("Don't bother trying to
decrypt a PreKey message with older sessions"; the exact upstream diff is
upstream-cd361186fba60c83186262d91b03af608fb8c7c3.diff next to this file) on the v0.105.4 tree.
The upstream diff does not reverse-apply there: commit 5cf8b0d71 ("Refactor 1:1 messaging code")
renamed rust/protocol/src/session_cipher.rs to session_cipher_legacy.rs and moved the live
decryption loop to `try_decrypt_from_record` in session_management.rs (later commits added
logging around the early return). Hunk by hunk:
  * rust/protocol/src/session_management.rs (the live code) and session_cipher_legacy.rs (the
    legacy copy libsignal keeps for its equivalence tests): upstream's `PreKey` early return
    removed, so a pre-key message that fails on the new session is tried on older sessions;
  * rust/protocol/tests/session.rs: upstream's added test `test_signedprekey_not_saved` removed.
git apply ignores this preamble.

